    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>After making several changes (now committed to trunk, to be included with Fedora 3.3 release) I was able to get this to work with SQL Server Express 2008 (WinXP/Java6/jTDS JDBC Driver v1.2.4)</p>\n\n<p>The Fedora installer doesn't currently support this option, so it must be configured manually.  Here's how I got it working:</p>\n\n<p>1) Install and configure SQL Server 2008 Express:<br/>\n  a) For \"sa\" (the default admin user), use \"fedoraAdmin1!\" as the password.<br/>\n  b) In the Sql Server Configuration Manager, under Network Configuration:<br/>\n     i) Enable TCP/IP<br/>\n     ii) Specify 1433 as the port for IPAll<br/>\n  c) Restart the database</p>\n\n<p>2) Download the jTDS JDBC Driver from <a href=\"http://jtds.sourceforge.net/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://jtds.sourceforge.net/</a></p>\n\n<p>3) Run the Fedora installer and select \"oracle\" (yes, oracle) as the install option.</p>\n\n<p>   Specify:<br/>\n   JDBC Driver Path: (the path to the jTDS jar you downloaded)<br/>\n   JDBC Driver Class: net.sourceforge.jtds.jdbc.Driver<br/>\n   JDBC URL: jdbc:jtds:sqlserver://localhost:1433<br/>\n   DB Username: sa<br/>\n   DB Password: fedoraAdmin1!</p>\n\n<p>4) After the installer has run, but before starting Fedora, modify<br/>\n   $FEDORA_HOME/server/config/fedora.fcfg</p>\n\n<p>   a) Change the backslash_is_escape parameter to \"false\"<br/>\n   b) Change all occurances of localOraclePool to localMSSQLPool<br/>\n   c) Within the datastore element with id \"localMSSQLPool\":<br/>\n      i) change the validationQuery value to \"select 1\"<br/>\n      ii) remove the connection.SetBigStringTryClob parameter</p>\n\n<p>5) Start Fedora for the first time</p>",
     "created": "14/Dec/09 12:56 PM",
     "id": "11164",
